there are certain wands which can affect a stack of items in one spell.
the size of the stack isn't a consideration (upto nh3.0f2, i haven't
studied this in nh3.0f3 yet). it may be better strategy to have these
wands only affect the top ten (or a few more randomly) items of a stack.
this change would nudge the game along the direction of cleverness without
making it harder.

wands of invisibility operate only on living things. could their effect also
get extended to inanimate objects? there are many ways to implement this,
two of which are: 1) invisible objects are out of sight and out of the game,
or 2) invisible objects are only accesible if you can see invisible (i.e.
leprechauns could not steal invisible gold). if you can't see invisible then
you have no knowledge of (or feelings about) invisible objects. can
invisibility be reversed? perhaps dipping into a cursed potion or casting
a cursed wand spell could accomplish this.

perhaps wands (and potions) of speed could also get extended to weapons
such that a sped (slowed) weapon is, let's say 20% more (less) effective.
dipping into quantum mechanic corpses would have an uncertain effect. of
course, a wizard would find a way to distill Q corpses into an appropriate
potion. this brings to mind the potion of liquid wax (non-existent!) which
can only come into existence by transmogrifying the fresh remains of certain
corrosive nasties ...
